Subject: Cantor Self Work Update Broker B1 CDrive Linked Worktree Preparation P0 Data Design

@ [data_design_uuid] 55915d54-3ee8-42b5-bf83-c2bbb3fddc99
@ [canonical_uuid] adb3d817-6198-489f-a037-48686d1d1f0a

& [Forms]
  + PreparationRequest carries exact source lineage constants identities topology environment budget and recovery owner
  + PreparationPlan carries ordered directory effects one exact Git effect closed observations and a domain digest
  + ProcessObservation carries sequence argv exit stdout stderr timeout interruption termination reaping descendants and late output
  + FilesystemObservation carries canonical role identities volume free bytes sentinels canary and forbidden-root account
  + GitObservation carries version top-level common-dir Git-dir HEAD branch status worktree and submodule facts
  + PreparationConsequences exhaust created roots refs metadata checkout processes and every required zero effect
  + PreparationReceipt carries only NotRun Quarantined or PreparedForPhase3AAcquisition with compatible physical-contact and mutation flags
  + PreparationFault carries one typed bounded code operation message resource account and retained-state truth

& [Determinism]
  + canonical compact JSON uses fixed field and vector order and rejects unknown duplicate or omitted fields
  + path case normalization is validation-only while receipt preserves exact canonical Windows spelling
  + receipt digest uses a new domain and excludes only its own digest field
  + wall-clock timestamps and measured elapsed time remain outside deterministic receipt identity

& [Bounds]
  + depth 32 fields 256 artifacts 16 per-file bytes 16777216 total bytes 67108864
  + process 12 per stream 1048576 total received 4194304 deadline 30000 milliseconds
  + tracked carrier count 4416 bytes 31972357 pre-free 15032385536 final-free 12884901888

& [NoSecretRule]
  + evidence contains environment names and hashes of fixed nonsecret values only
  + usernames appear only as the named recovery principal and no ambient credential value is recorded
